A||||10||Bruce||clutch pedal replacement||||1
Z||000000||Bruce||11-25-1999||11:16 AM||||Just bought a new (well, pretty new) steel clutch pedal from George at the Fiero Shop. Do I have to get all the bushings and washers that V8 Archie talks about, or can I use the existing ones.<BR>Happy Thanksgiving, forum!||||reg||1
Z||000001||David||11-25-1999||11:37 AM||||Get the bushing.  It takes up the space between the post on the pedal and the hole in the M/C pushrod.  GM part number 14094900 and just cost a couple of dollars (US).  When I last replaced the clutch M/C on my car I got the part from GM and the pushrod had a bushing in it that I had to remove so that it would fit over the post on my aluminum pedal.  Seems that the post on the aluminum pedal is a larger diameter than the post on the steel one, requiring the bushing when changing to steel.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-25-1999||02:16 PM||||You can get the bushing in a hardware store about $.75||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||11-25-1999||02:30 PM||||Whatz up, good to see your still with us. <P>Hope your little toy is doing ok.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bruce||11-25-1999||03:20 PM||||Where do I look for the bushing, or what do I ask for?<BR>Still here, Bill. Hope all is well with the assorted DXR's.||||reg||5
Z||000005||ggarsk||11-26-1999||02:07 AM||||You can find the bushings in the Motormite Help section at most part stores. The part # is 74016. It is for Fords but they do work. That is for the petal shaft. The other bushing you need you can get from a Hurst Shifters Pit Pack. I got some but I bet you don't want to wait for it to come via snail mail. If any one is going to change their petal let me know and I'll send you one. No charge.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shiner||11-26-1999||03:52 AM||||I heard that the clutch pedal is supposed to be about an inch higher than the brake pedal. I have the steel pedal (verified with magnet) on my '87 GT, but it's about EVEN with the brake pedal, and I am having some shifting problems (seems like I don't get enough travel)  Whats up with that?||||reg||5
Z||000007||Cooter||11-26-1999||11:03 AM||||According to V8 Archie, even the steel pedal can give problems over time. I used my "body shop discount" at the local Pontiac dealer and got my new steel pedal for $24. Even if it wasn't all of the problem, it was worth that much for the peace of mind of having the new pedal.||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||11-26-1999||11:08 AM||||When changing out the pedal its always a good idea to change out the stamped steel clutch arm. It is the same problem that they solved with the 87-88. Below 87 the arm is this thing that can be best described as a steel stip folded and welded to be pushed by the slave cylinder. The 87-88 had an actual cast (steel or iron Im not sure) arm that is just better.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bruce||11-26-1999||07:29 PM||||Where would I find that part?||||reg||5
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||11-27-1999||04:04 AM||||I got that part from FOCOA years ago but you might just ask for an 87-88 clutch arm from the dealer.||||reg||1
